Z||000004||Joe Torma||09-02-2001||03:09 PM||||I still can't figure out what you are trying to do?! Sorry!  If you are trying to remove the engine wiring harness, you need to remove the console and on that grey/black plastic thingie that the wires are glued into...there is a big plastic C clip you need to slide it out.  You have to unscrew the ADL connector too(2 screws).<P>Any closer to what you need to know??<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mickey_Moose||09-02-2001||03:38 PM||||I think he is talking about removing the harness from the firewall above the ECM?<P>I know they unplug, but as for removing the one set from the firewall - I'm not sure, they look glue into place.<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000006||Wolfhound||09-02-2001||06:48 PM||||From inside the car  behind the console there is a U shaped clip that has to be removed and it will come right out.||||reg||7
