Z||000010||Joe Torma||09-04-2001||03:52 AM||||You have to replace the whole wire?  You can't just solder in patches?<P>You have the harness removed from the firewall now right?  I assume, because you were able to open the plastic.  If you really want to remove/replace wires, spray the glue thoroughly with brake cleaner. Chip/pound with a hammer when the glue gets rock hard.  It will break apart...use more brake cleaner if necessary.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif"> <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm||||reg||1
Z||000011||DreXteR||09-04-2001||11:21 AM||||Yes, I have to replace all the cables. The moron that sells me the car use aluminum foil to insulate the cables!! He cook them!! Anyway most of the cables are ruin, and is better to replace it all.  <P>There is no plug to desconnect those wires??<P><BR>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000012||Joe Torma||09-04-2001||12:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DreXteR:<BR><B>Yes, I have to replace all the cables. The moron that sells me the car use aluminum foil to insulate the cables!! He cook them!! Anyway most of the cables are ruin, and is better to replace it all.  <P>There is no plug to desconnect those wires??<P><BR>DreX</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ALuminum foil insulation...nice.  The wires in that harness run from the computer/clear connectors under console to various engine components with no connectors in between.  That plastic firewall connector is just a big grommet.<P>||||reg||1
